                <pb facs="0979" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/102: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-20T16:00:00+00:00">December 20, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 20—1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. Department’s telegram No. 65, December 15, 2 p.m. received yesterday. Should
                    “formal protest” first paragraph be both oral and written? Action will be taken
                    on this paragraph on the receipt of reply to above question.</p>
                <p>Should many complicated questions in other paragraphs be taken up orally or in
                    writing? In either case request that Blake be ordered to Madrid either now or
                    immediately after Christmas as I consider his specialized and detailed knowledge
                    necessary for negotiations. Before replying please see my despatch 597 December
                        7.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d732-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
